          "location": {
            "kind": "File",
            "path": "bin\\NetFramework30ASPNETWEB.dll.config",
            "snippet": "\u003CconnectionStrings\u003E\r\n  \u003C!-- \r\n        Connection strings can be retrieved from Azure Key Vault for enhanced security.\r\n        \r\n        Option 1: Reference from Key Vault via App Settings (Azure App Service feature)\r\n        Example: @Microsoft.KeyVault(SecretUri=https://your-vault.vault.azure.net/secrets/SqlConnectionString/)\r\n        \r\n        Option 2: Retrieve programmatically using KeyVaultService\r\n        Example in code:\r\n            string connectionString = KeyVaultService.Instance.GetSecret(\u0022SqlConnectionString\u0022);\r\n            \r\n        DO NOT store actual connection strings with credentials here in production.\r\n        --\u003E\r\n\u003C/connectionStrings\u003E"
          }
